    description: "**Mechanism.** config-conventions.yaml:122-126 (cargo_dependency) and :175-178 (poetry_dependency) are byte-identical on their discriminators: both gate on symbol_kind '^dependency$' + language '^toml$'. The language gate is the FILE FORMAT (toml), not the dependency ECOSYSTEM; both Cargo.toml and pyproject.toml are TOML, so the gate cannot separate them and BOTH labels co-fire on every TOML dependency node. The YAML even acknowledges the producer routes both Cargo and Poetry tables through _extract_cargo_dependencies.\n\n**Evidence (frozen + live matcher).** meta.concepts census: config-conventions {cargo_dependency: 76, poetry_dependency: 76}. All 76 pyproject.toml dependency nodes carry BOTH (carry both 76 / only cargo 0 / only poetry 0); dependency nodes from Cargo.toml = 0; ZERO Cargo.toml files in the repo (it is a Python monorepo, 7 pyproject.toml). So all 76 cargo_dependency tags are false positives. Live: match_patterns(Symbol(kind=dependency, language=toml, name=rich, path=.../pyproject.toml), load_framework_patterns('config-conventions')) -> [cargo_dependency, poetry_dependency]. Symmetric: a genuine Cargo dep would equally get falsely tagged poetry_dependency.\n\n**Consequence.** A consumer reading meta.concepts to learn a package's ecosystem ('does this repo have Rust/Cargo deps?') is told YES (76 cargo_dependency) on a pure-Python repo; the two concepts carry zero discriminating info for TOML. A discriminator would need the filename (Cargo.toml vs pyproject.toml) or a meta key.\n\n**Related (distinct).** Same CLASS as WI-vuzur (framework-pattern language-gate causing concept FPs) but a DISTINCT framework (config-conventions), concept (cargo_dependency), and root: WI-vuzur is a MISSING per-pattern language gate; here the gate IS present but at the wrong granularity. Source: dogfood_tranche_07 F130.A1, frozen read + live-matcher repro."  # f4c7
    fields: {}  # f4c7
