  message: "Fixed in PR (dev 6da5a7cd38), Wave-3 Phase-2 §C linker F3. Root cause: cargo_* and poetry_* TOML-dependency patterns in config-conventions.yaml were byte-identical (symbol_kind '^dependency$' + language '^toml$') — TOML is a FORMAT not an ecosystem, so both fired on every pyproject.toml AND Cargo.toml dependency; the co-firing spanned the whole family (bare + dev + build), since the toml_config producer routes both ecosystems' dev tables through one kind+dependency_scope shape (verified: pyproject dev-dep fired cargo_dependency+cargo_dev_dependency+poetry_dependency+poetry_dev_dependency). Fix: symbol_path discriminator on all 5 patterns — cargo_* -> 'Cargo\\.toml$', poetry_* -> 'pyproject\\.toml$'. Behavioral evidence (editable binary, re-ran filed match_patterns repro on merged dev): pyproject.toml dep vs config-conventions = ['poetry_dependency'] (was ['cargo_dependency','poetry_dependency']); Cargo.toml dep = ['cargo_dependency']. Production-path tests: test_framework_patterns.py::TestFrameworkPatternEcosystemGating (4 cargo/poetry cases incl. dev variants). 861 framework_patterns tests pass, 100% coverage. No bakeoff tag: deterministic FP elimination verified by the match_patterns repro + tests, not an uncertain bakeoff-corpus metric movement."  # 2ef4
